### Setup

Let $\mathfrak{g} = \mathfrak{sl}_{n+1}(\mathbb{C})$, the Lie algebra of traceless $(n+1)\times(n+1)$ matrices. Its Cartan subalgebra is
$$\mathfrak{h} = \{\, h = \operatorname{diag}(h_1, \dots, h_{n+1}) : h_1 + \cdots + h_{n+1} = 0 \,\}.$$

For $1 \le i,j \le n+1$, let $E_{ij}$ denote the elementary matrix with $1$ in position $(i,j)$ and $0$ elsewhere. The standard commutator computation gives, for $h \in \mathfrak{h}$,
$$[h, E_{ij}] = (h_i - h_j)\, E_{ij}. \tag{1}$$

The simple positive roots of $\mathfrak{sl}_{n+1}$ (type $A_n$) are
$$\alpha_i(h) = h_i - h_{i+1}, \qquad i = 1, \dots, n,$$
corresponding to the root vectors $E_{i,\,i+1}$.

### The candidate

Set
$$\boxed{x_\theta \;=\; E_{1,\,n+1},}$$
the elementary matrix with a single $1$ in position $(1, n+1)$.

### Verification

For any $h = \operatorname{diag}(h_1, \dots, h_{n+1}) \in \mathfrak{h}$, by (1):
$$[h, x_\theta] = [h, E_{1,n+1}] = (h_1 - h_{n+1})\, E_{1,n+1} = (h_1 - h_{n+1})\, x_\theta. \tag{2}$$

Now compute the weight $(\alpha_1 + \cdots + \alpha_n)(h)$:
$$(\alpha_1 + \cdots + \alpha_n)(h) = \sum_{i=1}^{n} \alpha_i(h) = \sum_{i=1}^{n} (h_i - h_{i+1}) = h_1 - h_{n+1}, \tag{3}$$
since the sum telescopes.

Combining (2) and (3):
$$[h, x_\theta] = (h_1 - h_{n+1})\, x_\theta = (\alpha_1 + \cdots + \alpha_n)(h)\, x_\theta \qquad \text{for all } h \in \mathfrak{h}.$$

### Remark

The weight $\theta := \alpha_1 + \cdots + \alpha_n$ is the **highest root** of $\mathfrak{sl}_{n+1}$; it corresponds to the functional $e_1 - e_{n+1}$. The matrix $E_{1,n+1}$ is the standard root vector for this highest root, so it is the natural (and up to scalar, the unique) element $x_\theta \in \mathfrak{sl}_{n+1}$ satisfying the required eigenvalue equation. $\blacksquare$

